quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  9,1,
  9,2,(This is) a (declaration of) acquittal from Allah and His Messenger (addressed) to those (Meccan) polytheists with whom you had made a treaty (of peace and they breached it).
  9,3,(O breachers of the peace!) You may (still) travel freely in the land for four months (as a truce period) and know that you cannot escape Allah (by frustrating Him). And Allah will disgrace the disbelievers (who persecuted the peaceful civilians).
  9,4,"(This is) a proclamation from Allah and His Messenger to the people on the Day of the Great Pilgrimage that Allah and His Messenger are absolved from all obligations to the (peace breaching) polytheists.* So, if you repent, it would be better for you. But if you turn away, know that you cannot escape Allah. And warn the (persecuting) disbelievers of a painful punishment."
  9,5,"Except for those polytheists with whom you made a treaty and who did not breach any of its terms with you, nor did they support anyone against you. So, fulfil the treaty with them until the end of their term. Indeed, Allah loves the God-conscious."
  9,6,"So when the forbidden months are over, kill the (combatant) idolaters (those who have initiated a war against you) wherever you find them (on the battlefield), or capture them and imprison them, or lie in wait for them at every place of ambush (to besiege them). But, if they repent (after being taken as prisoners of war), and they perform the prayer and give the alms due, then leave their way open (by releasing them). Indeed, Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
